From a3459caaa3fc55fa78e3a4dd78ed49526134d37c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: li-yiyang <yiyang.li.11pro@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:09:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-msm: clear stale after the SDR50 attach

o2->stale is set when a calibrated phase stops reading on a registered
card and is only cleared in o2_forget_card() (a CID change) or at probe.
With the same card the gate therefore stays closed and the card remains on
SDR50 until a rebind or reboot, even though the stored phase may read again.

Clear the flag when the SDR50 path is taken: the attach that clamped stays
at 100 MHz, the next attach runs on SDR50, and the attach after that
re-scores the stored phase and returns to SDR104.  A forced host-tuning
failure and a genuinely bad phase still end on SDR50, as before.

Tested on a TB323FU with the Lenovo 58.6 GiB card: three forced-miss rounds
(12 s2idle resumes) each went 100 MHz clamp -> SDR50 -> 202 MHz, and a
full_sweep=1 build hit an unforced miss and clamped the same way.

Signed-off-by: li-yiyang <yiyang.li.11pro@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sd-retimer-o2.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sd-retimer-o2.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sd-retimer-o2.c
index 38fef47..e62ff0c 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sd-retimer-o2.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sd-retimer-o2.c
@@ -658,6 +658,7 @@ void o2_retimer_init_card(struct o2_retimer *o2, struct mmc_host *mmc,
 	return;
 
 sdr50:
+	o2->stale = false;	/* one SDR50 attach, retry on the next */
 	mmc->caps &= ~MMC_CAP_UHS_SDR104;
 }
 
